{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Hemolytic", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (57.14%) to AI predicted Peptide 3967 I: 15%, L: 23%, R: 31%. Activity: active against S. aureus ATCC 25923 (MIC50 11.0 uM, MIC90 148.9 uM), E. faecalis ATCC 29212 (MIC50 0.70 uM), MIC90 107.2 uM), P. aeruginosa ATCC 27853 (MIC50 4.1 uM; MIC90 28.5 uM), E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC50 14.2 uM, MIC90 69.4 uM). Structure: random coil in water and helical in 30% TFE. In vitro toxicity: human RBC: HC50 17 uM, hemolytic. Cytotoxicity: HaCaT cells (TC50>100 uM), breast cancer cells MCF7 (12% at 100 uM).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "33919639", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Pharmaceutics. 2021 Apr 18;13(4):578. doi: 10.3390/pharmaceutics13040578. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP05625", "source_id": "AP05625", "source_numeric_id": "05625", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP05625", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "In Silico Selection and Evaluation of Pugnins with Antibacterial and Anticancer Activity Using Skin Transcriptome of Treefrog (Boana pugnax).", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Hemolytic", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (71.43%) to Pugnin A I: 15%, L: 23%, R: 31%. Activity: active against S. aureus ATCC 25923 (MIC50 9.2 uM, MIC90 549.7 uM), E. faecalis ATCC 29212 (MIC50 18.0 uM), MIC90 111.2 uM), P. aeruginosa ATCC 27853 (MIC50 8.9 uM; MIC90 158.4 uM), E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC50 0.10 uM, MIC90 57.8 uM). Structure: random coil in water and helical in 30% TFE. In vitro toxicity: human RBC: HC50 32 uM, hemolytic. Cytotoxicity: HaCaT cells (TC50 <100 uM), breast cancer cells MCF7 (5% at 100 uM).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "33919639", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Pharmaceutics. 2021 Apr 18;13(4):578. doi: 10.3390/pharmaceutics13040578. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP05626", "source_id": "AP05626", "source_numeric_id": "05626", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP05626", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "In Silico Selection and Evaluation of Pugnins with Antibacterial and Anticancer Activity Using Skin Transcriptome of Treefrog (Boana pugnax).", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
